00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:38.340
in 2026. Most Canadian investors still treat their TFSA, RRSP, FHSA, and RESP as four completely

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.820
separate buckets. They contribute to whichever account feels convenient that month,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.800
then throw similar types of investments into all of them. That, in my view, is the first

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.700
and most expensive mistake. The real power comes from treating these accounts as an integrated

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:58.300
rules-based system where every asset is deliberately located, where it will be most tax-efficient

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:03.740
over time. Here's the exact contribution hierarchy I recommend for new capital in 2026.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.580
First, if you are still eligible for the first home savings account and you realistically plan to

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.960
buy a home within the next 15 years, max out your FHSA before you do anything else.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.940
The triple tax advantage here is hard to beat. You get a deductible contribution today,

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.680
tax-free growth inside the account, and if used for a qualifying first home purchase,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:31.020
a completely tax-free withdrawal. That combination makes the FHSA the highest-octane vehicle

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.860
available to eligible Canadians right now. Second, once the FHSA is topped up or you're no longer

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:43.320
eligible, fill your TFSA to the new 2026 cumulative limit. For someone who has never contributed before,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.720
that room now sits at approximately $102,000. Inside the TFSA, we want to house your

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:55.060
highest growth most tax- inefficient assets, think growth stocks with very low or no dividends,

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:01.160
thematic ETFs, crypto ETFs, small cap momentum names, and even certain covered call strategies

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:06.600
that generate frequent short-term capital gains. Because all growth and income inside a TFSA

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:11.240
is completely tax-free on withdrawal, this account should be your aggressive growth engine.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:18.080
Third, turn your attention to the RRSP, especially if your marginal tax rate is 40% or higher.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:23.980
The immediate tax deduction makes the RRSP extremely powerful for anyone in a high tax bracket.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.640
Inside the RRSP, we want to place tax-efficient income generators,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.260
Canadian dividend aristocrats that pay eligible dividends, preferred shares, bonds,

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.920
corporate debt, and any assets producing foreign dividends or interest income.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:46.820
The RRSP is also the ideal home for broad US total market ETFs because it shields you from the 15%

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:53.100
US withholding tax that would otherwise apply inside a TFSA. Fourth, for families with children,

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:59.520
the RRSP should be used aggressively because of the government grants. The Canada Education Savings Grant

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.980
provides an immediate 20% match on the first two dollars, 500 contributed annually,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:12.840
up to $500 per child per year, that is essentially free money. Inside the RRSP, we bias toward globally

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:18.600
diversified balanced growth ETFs and target date style funds that automatically reduce volatility

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:24.780
as the child gets closer to post-secondary education. Let's talk about the asset location rules

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:30.940
that actually move the needle in 2026. Your TFSA should function as the pure tax-efficient growth

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:38.500
engine of your household. Ideal holdings include ARKK style innovation and disruptive technology, ETFs,

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.060
emerging market small cap exposure, Bitcoin and Ethereum ETFs,

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:48.420
carefully risk-managed leveraged sector ETFs, and individual high beta growth stocks that you

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:53.680
believe have multi-year compounding potential. Every capital gain, dividend, and interest payment

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.800
generated here is 100% tax-free when withdrawn. That's an enormous advantage most investors

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:05.120
still underutilize. Conversely, your RRSP should be the tax-efficient income and foreign exposure

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:12.040
engine. Here you want US total market or S&amp;P 500 ETFs to avoid that 15% withholding tax drag.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:17.320
Canadian banks, utilities, and preferred shares that generate eligible dividends fit beautifully

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:21.480
because the gross up and dividend tax credit work well inside a registered account.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:27.620
Corporate bonds, GICs, and any interest-producing assets also belong in the RRSP,

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.600
where the interest is deferred rather than taxed annually at your marginal rate.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:38.480
Treat your FHSA like a supercharged TFSA specifically earmarked for the home purchase goal,

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:45.300
a 7030 or 8020 equity mix between Canadian and US broad market ETFs is usually appropriate

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.780
given the shorter time horizon. Importantly, once you purchase the qualifying home,

